From f0e7b682fa06ffe8e3e877c011200665849a7daf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rohan8504 <102684130+Rohan8504@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:24:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: AI admission agent with tool calling, 6 languages
 and public data

Agent (server/services/agent)
- The chatbot is now a tool-calling agent. Tools: search_knowledge_base,
  check_eligibility, list_upcoming_events, register_for_event,
  get_my_application_status, request_counselling, lookup_pincode and
  analyze_github_profile. Tools act only for the signed-in student.
- Providers: Claude via the official @anthropic-ai/sdk tool runner
  (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY), Gemini function calling (GEMINI_API_KEY), and an
  offline rule-based planner that uses the same tools when no key is set
  or the LLM call fails. AGENT_PROVIDER forces one.
- The chat response now includes the tools used, shown as "Agent
  actions" chips in the UI.

Multilingual
- English, Hindi, Tamil, Telugu, Kannada and Malayalam: language picker,
  script detection, localized UI strings and offline replies, native
  keyword mapping for search, and voice input via the Web Speech API.

Public data
- India Post pincode directory: registration auto-fills city/state
  (GET /api/public/pincode/:pincode) and the agent can look up pincodes.
- GitHub public API: profile review with an indicative readiness score
  for the Young Innovator Scholarship.

Also
- Event registration and counselling logic moved to studentActions.js and
  shared by the REST routes and the agent; ticket numbers use crypto
  randomness to avoid collisions.
- /chat only continues a conversation that belongs to the student.
- Floating assistant hidden on the full assistant page (it covered the
  input bar).
- 40 new tests, including the Claude provider against a local mock API.
